role: llm.format.ison
response_format: text
---
The data below is encoded in ISON (Indented Sparse Object Notation), a compact
table format. Read it like this:

- `table.<path>` introduces a table. The next line is its header row
  (space-separated column names); every line after that is one record with
  the values in header order.
- `null` is an empty value, `[]` an empty list.
- A list of records inside a field becomes its own table
  `table.<path>_<field>`. Its column `records_id` points back to the parent
  record — `:1` is the first record of the parent table.

Example:

table.records
title score aliases
Introduction 0.5 null
Background 0.9 []

table.records_aliases
records_id value
:1 a
:1 b
